[09:55:04] ## What changed
[09:55:04] **New `frontend/scripts/bundleFreshness.mjs`** — `requireFreshBundle()` refuses to let a browser check start unless `frontend/dist/` can stand as evidence about the current source, and otherwise returns the comparison for the caller to print. Three rejections, each naming the file and both timestamps plus the build instruction:
[09:55:04] 1. output missing (`dist/index.html` absent),
[09:55:04] 2. output incomplete (the emitted document references a same-origin file `dist/` doesn't contain),
[09:55:04] 3. output stale (any build input — `index.html`, `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, `public/`, `src/` recursively, `tsconfig.json`, `vite.config.ts` — modified later than `dist/index.html`).
[09:55:04] It requires the build rather than performing one, so the check stays a report on what the developer has.
[09:55:04] **The seven dist-serving smoke scripts** (`sync`, `layout`, `profit`, `icon`, `discovery`, `ecto`, `favicon`) replaced the shared `existsSync(…index.html)` guard with that call and print a `Bundle  : …` header line. No browser/API assertion, step name or step count changed. The other scripts (`smoke:browser`, `smoke:account`, the three `*:live` checks, `check:icons:live`, `perf:profit-page`) never read `dist` — they open an operator-started origin — so they had no such guard to fix.
[09:55:04] Also: `frontend/scripts/__tests__/bundleFreshness.spec.mjs`, one `test.include` line in `vite.config.ts`, and the methodology rule in `docs/TEST_STRATEGY.md` §12.2.
[09:55:04] ## Tests run
[09:55:04] - `npx vitest run scripts/__tests__/bundleFreshness.spec.mjs` — `Tests 7 passed (7)`
[09:55:04] - `npm test` — `Test Files 22 passed (22) | Tests 302 passed (302)` (the include change affects collection)
[09:55:04] - `npm run build` — `✓ built in 442ms`
[09:55:04] - Controls on the shipped files: touching only `src/App.vue`'s mtime made `ecto-browser-smoke.mjs` exit 1 with `frontend/dist is stale: src/App.vue was modified …, after dist/index.html was built …`; with `dist/` moved aside, `favicon-browser-smoke.mjs` exit 1 with `frontend/dist/index.html is missing`.
[09:55:04] - Against the current build: `smoke:ecto` PASSED (6), `smoke:favicon` PASSED (7), `smoke:sync` PASSED (8), `smoke:icons` PASSED (10).
[09:55:04] - `smoke:layout`, `smoke:profit`, `smoke:discovery` passed the guard and then failed further on for pre-existing reasons (stale `sync-controls` selector; a `For one craft` expectation the component's own spec forbids; `> legend` queries against `div`s). Each reproduced identically with a throwaway `git show HEAD:…` copy of the committed script, so the guard is not the cause; the copies were deleted and `git status` lists none.
[09:55:04] Those three are recorded as F002–F004 (plus F001: `scripts/.tmp-control-unrelated-call.mjs` is tracked in git; F005: an orphaned backlog summary line) in the story and `CLAUDE_RESULT.md`. Story status, backlog row and result are updated; nothing was committed.
